{"request_sha256": "9817453e2e6d722f71e7eeca208a33f10b210eda25a0b18c890e435a76e5ca4e", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "93509ceffb5d38fa0a331d539b3ec6e26f06e0bf929cfca08ae1a48196f3a50d", "schema_sha256": "b11348cd1fb9f87dee1f7d8b64746455da08f64a4885c641943f00ea25a47f5f", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 7552}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["render-0 and render-1 (P-WHOLE, seeds 1 and 42): the crown is a small, spherical starburst of thin, short, nearly straight wire-like fronds. It is not a rosette of long arching pinnate fronds whose lowest fronds droop, as in reference-0 and reference-1. The frond length and leaflet size problems the owner named are still visible.", "render-0: the trunk is strongly wavy, with a pronounced multi-bend S-curve through the upper half. render-1: the trunk has several kinks and bends in its upper half. Both break the owner's rule that the trunk must be straight or gently leaning and never wavy.", "render-2 (P-TRUNK): the trunk is smooth, with sparse, isolated, rounded knob stubs. There is no dense spiral diamond or rhomboid lattice of wedge-shaped leaf bases and no fibrous matting, unlike reference-1 and reference-2.", "render-3 (P-BASE): what is drawn is a smooth dark trunk surface with one or two isolated rounded knobs. It does not show the close-range lattice of flat-faced leaf-base stubs packed with fibre seen in reference-2. The metadata marks this view's visibility as 'hidden', even though a trunk surface is plainly rendered.", "render-2: the fronds read as thin rachis lines with tiny leaflets. They lack the full-bodied, V-sectioned, bristly silhouette of reference-1."], "observations": ["Both seeds show one unbranched trunk with a crown at the apex. No branches and no foliage or epiphytes are drawn on the trunk; only the leaf-base knobs appear.", "Trunk diameter is roughly constant apart from a flared foot at the ground in render-0 and render-1. That flare broadly matches the basal widening in reference-0.", "reference-0 shows a leaning trunk curved at the base, which the inventory records as variation. The owner's requirement (never wavy) takes priority, and the render's repeated mid-trunk waves differ from the reference's single lean with a basal curve.", "The finish level (flat shading, clean silhouette) is broadly in line with the spruce anchor-0. The failures are morphological, not a matter of finish.", "No fruit clusters are rendered. The date cluster (fn-111) is not landed."], "findings": [{"observation": "Crown fronds in both seeds are short, thin and radiate straight in every direction, including straight down. There is no arching curve and no drooping lower skirt. The crown's spread is only about 2-3 times the trunk width at the apex, and the crown is small relative to trunk height, unlike reference-0's large drooping hemisphere.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and leaflet size dials may still be too low, and there appears to be no gravity-driven arching along the rachis."}, {"observation": "The trunk is wavy, with several opposing bends: a strong S in seed 1 and repeated kinks in seed 42.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The stem's curvature or noise settings may still be active on the palm trunk. The trunk's taper value (1.0) is outside the dial table, but that dial concerns diameter, not waviness."}, {"observation": "The trunk surface shows sparse, isolated knob stubs on a smooth cylinder. There is no tessellating spiral diamond lattice and no fibre filling between the stubs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No growth appears on the trunk in either seed. The only features between the base and the crown are leaf-base stubs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The stem is single, unbranched and close to constant in diameter, with a basal flare.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Fruit clusters are absent from the render. In the references, fruit appears only in reference-0; the visible crown in reference-1 shows none. It is therefore unclear whether fruit is defining (core) or a seasonal state.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "The date cluster organ (fn-111) is not landed."}, {"observation": "The P-BASE view metadata says visibility 'hidden', but the image shows a clipped close-up of the trunk surface. It is unclear whether this frame is the intended base view, because no ground contact is visible.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Differences in foliage colour and trunk lean are covered by the variation traits and are not treated as defects.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The render's crown is a small, spherical starburst of short, straight, thin fronds with no arching or recurving. The references show a large rosette of long arching fronds with a drooping lower tier."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The leaflets are tiny and the fronds read as thin wire lines. The plumose, V-sectioned, bristly frond body seen in reference-1 and reference-2 is absent."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The render has sparse, isolated, rounded knobs on a smooth trunk rather than a dense spiral diamond lattice of flat-faced wedge stubs. Following the caveat, I judged only what is drawn, and it does not match."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The trunk surface between the knobs is smooth and uniform. There is none of the shaggy reddish-brown fibre that fills the lattice in the references."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "One unbranched stem of near-constant diameter carries the crown. The waviness is failed separately under the owner's straight-trunk priority."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The render has no fruit. Fruit appears only in reference-0, and the crown visible in reference-1 has none, so the inventory's core rating looks like a seasonal state and is contested. The fn-111 cluster is not landed. The core status cannot be confirmed from these references, so the result is unknown."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-8